# Dev API target for the Vite proxy (see vite.config.ts). Defaults to the local
# Python API. The browser talks to the SPA's own origin; Vite proxies /v1 + /health.
VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# --- Frontend (Vite dev server) --------------------------------------------
# Hosts the dev server will answer for. EMPTY BY DEFAULT: Vite refuses a request
# whose Host header it does not recognise (DNS-rebinding protection), so serving
# the UI through any reverse proxy needs the proxy's hostname here or every
# request 403s before routing. A leading dot matches subdomains. localhost and
# 127.0.0.1 are always allowed. Set in frontend/.env (gitignored), not here.
#VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=.example.org
